I walk over to the fruit and vegetables.
There are many beautiful colors.
I take a red apple.
"I like apples," I think.
I smell the apple.
I put the apple in my shopping cart.
I also take some tomatoes.
And I choose a green cucumber.
Then I see a strange vegetable.
I don't know it from Mexico.
I pick it up.
I turn it over.
"What is that?" I think.
I put the vegetable back.
Maybe another day.
